    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, can u explain what the seller is actually responsible for under CIF Incoterms 2020? need to make sure our contract for this electronics shipment is solid.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF Incoterms 2020, the seller is responsible for arranging and paying for the main carriage of the goods to the named port of destination. Crucially, the seller must also arrange and pay for the insurance covering the goods up to that destination port. Risk transfers from the seller to the buyer when the goods are loaded onto the vessel at the port of shipment. Therefore, the seller handles transport and insurance costs until the goods are safely loaded.",
      "source": "target",
